.SH NAME
blast-inspect - Analyze the blast radius of a file or directory


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBblast inspect  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Analyze a file's direct and indirect dependents within the JS/TS module
graph, plus Git history, relevant CI workflows, and an explainable risk
score. Given a directory (e.g. "blast inspect ." or "blast inspect src"),
every JS/TS module inside it is analyzed and reported as a risk-sorted
summary instead of one full per-file report.  defaults to "."
(the current directory) if omitted. See "blast --help" for the v0.1
module-resolution scope and limitations.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--explain\fP[=false]
	ask a local Ollama model to explain the risk in natural language (single-file target only; requires Ollama running locally)

.PP
\fB--explain-host\fP=""
	Ollama host (default: $OLLAMA_HOST or http://localhost:11434)

.PP
\fB--explain-model\fP=""
	Ollama model to use (default: llama3.2)

.PP
\fB--fail-on\fP=""
	exit with code 2 if risk is at or above this level (low, medium, high)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for inspect

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	write the report to this file instead of stdout


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBblast(1)\fP


